    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0605" n="591" xml:id="pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/2428</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-04">April 4, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hull</hi>: You will recall that on March
                    20th I left with you an <hi rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi><anchor n="35a"
                        xml:id="d350-f1"/> about the application of the principle of unconditional
                    surrender to minor Axis European States, explaining that a similar approach was
                    being made to the Soviet Government. I now enclose a copy of a telegram from our
                    Ambassador at Moscow<anchor n="36" xml:id="d350-f2"/> giving the reply of the
                    Soviet Government.</p>
                <p>Can you now tell me anything more about the United States position?</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d350-f1" n="35a" xml:id="d350-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d350-f2" n="36" xml:id="d350-f2-content">
                <p>Dated March 30, not printed; it gave substance of the communication quoted in
                    memorandum from the Soviet Embassy, March 31, <ref target="#pg586">p.
                    586</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
